## 📄 `man_1_simple_shell`

```man
.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "December 2025" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Simple Shell is a basic UNIX command interpreter that executes commands read
from standard input. It works in both interactive and non-interactive modes.

The shell creates child processes to execute commands using execve and waits
for them to terminate before continuing execution.

.SH FEATURES
- Command execution via fork and execve
- PATH resolution
- Interactive and non-interactive usage
- Environment inheritance

.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
($) /bin/ls
($) exit
.fi

Non-interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success. Returns non-zero on failure.

.SH AUTHORS
Kevin Galarza Arzon  
Anthony Caban

.SH SEE ALSO
sh(1), execve(2), fork(2), wait(2)
